WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.068
Welcome to Flexion, a research prototype that helps a clinician review how someone moves,

2
00:00:06.068 --> 00:00:08.820
using only the camera on a laptop or tablet.

3
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.129
This short guide shows you how to complete the routine.

4
00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:16.268
Before you begin, set up a safe space.

5
00:00:16.718 --> 00:00:20.198
You will need a laptop or tablet with a camera, a stable chair,

6
00:00:20.198 --> 00:00:24.893
and enough clear room to step back so that your whole body, from shoulders to ankles,

7
00:00:24.893 --> 00:00:25.998
fits in the picture.

8
00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:30.245
If you can, have someone with you, and keep any walking aid within reach.

9
00:00:30.695 --> 00:00:34.458
If you are using a MacBook, turn off Center Stage in Control Center,

10
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:38.055
because it can zoom in on your face and crop out the rest of you.

11
00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:43.564
Open the Flexion website and choose Try the Patient Capture Demo,

12
00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:45.992
or Patient Capture in the menu at the top.

13
00:00:46.442 --> 00:00:49.949
Nothing needs to be installed, and no video is uploaded.

14
00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.205
All of the analysis happens inside your own browser.

15
00:00:54.955 --> 00:00:59.008
On the capture page, you can type a name. This is for the demo only.

16
00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:04.468
Use the walking aid menu to say whether you use a stick, a frame, or another aid today,

17
00:01:04.468 --> 00:01:08.269
so that the instructions and the results can take it into account.

18
00:01:08.719 --> 00:01:13.288
Leave the advanced movements box unticked unless a clinician has asked for them.

19
00:01:13.288 --> 00:01:15.801
They are meant for fitter or younger people.

20
00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:21.329
When you are ready, press Start Routine, and choose Allow when your browser asks to use the camera.

21
00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:26.630
The app then reads each instruction aloud and shows it on screen,

22
00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.924
with a count of which movement you are on.

23
00:01:29.374 --> 00:01:31.955
There are four movements in the default routine.

24
00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:36.204
Step back until your whole body is visible. If the app cannot see you,

25
00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:38.592
it will ask you to step back into the frame.

26
00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:44.246
First, sit in a stable chair, with your arms crossed if that is safe.

27
00:01:44.696 --> 00:01:49.091
Stand fully upright and sit back down five times, as briskly as is safe.

28
00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:52.783
If you need your hands to push up, do it the way you normally would.

29
00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:59.333
Second, raise both arms overhead and lower them, three times, at a comfortable pace.

30
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:03.858
If you cannot stand safely without your walking aid, sit down for this one.

31
00:02:05.608 --> 00:02:09.765
Third, stand with your feet together and your arms relaxed at your sides.

32
00:02:09.765 --> 00:02:12.157
Hold as steady as you can for ten seconds.

33
00:02:12.607 --> 00:02:16.533
Stay near a wall or a sturdy chair in case you need to steady yourself.

34
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:20.609
If you use a walking aid, only do this one with someone beside you.

35
00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:26.050
Fourth, march on the spot, lifting your knees, for fifteen seconds.

36
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:29.145
Stand next to a sturdy surface that you can hold.

37
00:02:30.895 --> 00:02:33.425
If the app loses sight of you part way through,

38
00:02:33.425 --> 00:02:36.762
it will say tracking lost and ask you to step back into frame.

39
00:02:37.212 --> 00:02:41.713
Check that your whole body is visible and that the room is well lit, then carry on.

40
00:02:42.163 --> 00:02:45.513
Stop at any time if a movement feels unsafe or painful.

41
00:02:47.263 --> 00:02:50.036
At the end you will see a summary in plain language.

42
00:02:50.486 --> 00:02:52.769
It tells you which movements were completed,

43
00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:55.883
and whether anything was flagged for a clinician to look at.

44
00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:59.917
It is not a diagnosis, and it cannot tell you that you are well.

45
00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:05.724
Share the results with the GP, physiotherapist or clinical team who asked you to do them.

46
00:03:05.724 --> 00:03:11.141
Contact them sooner if you have had a fall, feel unsteady, or had pain during any movement.

47
00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:16.731
Clinicians can open the Provider Dashboard to review saved sessions.

48
00:03:17.181 --> 00:03:22.493
Each result shows a key metric, an evidence tier, moderate or exploratory, and any flags.

49
00:03:22.943 --> 00:03:25.303
The sessions shown here are sample data,

50
00:03:25.303 --> 00:03:29.257
and in this prototype the data stays in the browser on that device.

51
00:03:31.007 --> 00:03:32.778
That is the whole routine.

52
00:03:33.228 --> 00:03:36.936
Flexion is a research prototype. It is not a medical device,

53
00:03:36.936 --> 00:03:39.841
and it has not been validated for clinical use.

54
00:03:40.291 --> 00:03:41.742
Thank you for watching.

